<title>USA: Hearing set on BA, American alliance.</title>
<headline>Hearing set on BA, American alliance.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Senate Antitrust subcommittee said Monday it would hold a hearing April 22 on the alliance between British Airways Plc and AMR Corp unit American Airlines.</p>
<p>&quot;This proposed alliance has far-reaching effects on international business or personal travelers, and should be thoroughly explored before a final decision is made,&quot; panel chairman Mike DeWine, R-Ohio, said in a statement.</p>
<p>He said the alliance would allow two of the world's largest airlines to fix prices and schedules and allocate capacity in the U.S. to Britain market with immunity from U.S. antitrust laws. Witnesses will include airline officials.</p>
</text>
